  "question": {
    "text": "Based on the equation:\n$$\n\\Delta \\mathrm{E}=-2.0 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_2^2}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_1^2}\\right)\n$$\nthe wavelength of the light that must be absorbed to excite hydrogen electron from level $n=1$ to level $\\mathrm{n}=2$ will be: $\\left(\\mathrm{h}=6.625 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}, \\mathrm{C}=3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QTslS",
      "text": "\n$1.325 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WiDcT",
      "text": "\n$1.325 \\times 10^{-10} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
